# Ryan Rix - redirects (Cloudflare Pages)
# Rules are matched in order; first match wins.
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/

# --- Channel entry points (2026-10-01) ---
# Why these exist: X, Facebook and Substack all rewrite outbound links through their own
# redirectors, so a ?src= parameter on a link we hand them can be lost. A bare path on OUR
# domain cannot be stripped - the tracking is applied on our side of the boundary.
# Use these in bios, welcome emails, newsletter footers, anywhere the platform mediates the click.
#
# Namespacing: RR uses the rr* prefix (rrx / rrfb / rrsub) so these can never be confused with
# The Basics Hub's un-prefixed tokens (x / fb / fbgroup / substack) in MailerLite's msource field.
/substack https://ryanrix.com/?src=rrsub 301
/x https://ryanrix.com/?src=rrx 301
/fb https://ryanrix.com/?src=rrfb 301
